  "stdAdapter": "One identical scalar target and inverse neutral-luminance curve per RGB input channel, followed by the serialized exported VLOG cube with tetrahedral interpolation. A spans the reachable native black/white range in linear light; B retains identity through 18% linear gray and rolls highlights to reachable white. B saturates below the native black floor. Renderer output RGB is unchanged; no neutral subtraction, chroma gain, OKLab bounds or new output gamut mapping. Fixed per LUT, not per image and not a measured camera inverse.",
